// Warning 2's own fingerprint, alongside mid/form/unique/canon/'s: the same
// idea (a function's own variables become positions, everything else stays
// verbatim), except a literal fingerprints by its KIND alone, not its value --
// "I", not "I10" -- so two functions that differ only in a literal collide
// here even though mid/form/unique/'s duplicate-logic rule (which keeps the
// value) does not treat them as one function written twice. Reused as-is:
// canon_var, canon_callee, canon_params, decl_tag, decl_name, sep_at, bin_op,
// uq_begin, cn -- none of them touch a literal or reach into a nested call
// the strict chain would not already have canonicalised, so there is nothing
// for the loose walk to do differently there.
//
// It does NOT fold an identity operation (mid/form/unique/canon/expr/more/
// const/) or abstract which import a function reads: neither is needed by
// the examples docs/PROJECT.md's "decomposition warnings" section measures,
// and skipping them keeps this module a fraction of the strict one's size.
// A function containing a node kind this walk does not recognise (`un`,
// `index`, `arr`, `if`, `while`, `iassign`) fingerprints with its own node id
// in the tag (lz_e4/lz_st2), which cannot equal any other function's -- it is
// simply never flagged, not flagged wrongly.

lz_expr(int id) {
  string out = lz_e2(id);
  if(k_of(id) == "int") {
    out = "I";
  }
  if(k_of(id) == "float") {
    out = "F";
  }
} return string out;
given lz_fixture ((import lz_id_a)):("I")
given lz_fixture ((import lz_id_b)):("I")

lz_e2(int id) {
  string out = lz_e3(id);
  if(k_of(id) == "str") {
    out = "S";
  }
  if(k_of(id) == "var") {
    out = canon_var(id);
  }
} return string out;

lz_e3(int id) {
  string out = lz_e4(id);
  if(k_of(id) == "import") {
    out = "g(" + s1_of(id) + ")";
  }
  if(k_of(id) == "bin") {
    out = lz_bin(id);
  }
} return string out;
